  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Unseasonable warmth through the rest of the week\n\n-  Cold front Friday brings widespread gusty winds, transitioning\n   to a much cooler, breezy, and showery weekend.\n\n\n\nAbove-normal temperatures and dry conditions will persist today \ninto Thursday under southwesterly flow aloft. On Friday, a trough\nof low pressure will dig south along the West Coast, then move\ninland across the Northern Rockies. A cold front associated with\nthe trough will pass through the Northern Rockies on Friday\nafternoon through Saturday morning, bringing a sharp decrease in \ntemperatures for Saturday and strong winds with the frontal \npassage. Some concerns with this system will be the strong winds\ncreating choppy conditions on area lakes, an increase in fire\nweather concerns (also due to strong winds), and freezing \novernight low temperatures starting on Sunday morning for some \nhigher elevation communities.\n\nThe weekend system will also bring precipitation with it. \nGuidance continues to favor a more northerly track for the low, \nfocusing the most widespread rainfall across northwest Montana \nand the Idaho Panhandle. Snow levels lower to around 6,000 feet \nnear the center of the low's track, introducing winter- like \nbackcountry impacts to the higher terrain, particularly Glacier \nNational Park. Seasonably cool temperatures will follow, bringing \nclearing skies and frosty mornings early next week.",
